\chapter{URL Shortener}

\section{Problem Statement}
Design a service that shortens long URLs and redirects efficiently.

\section{Requirements}
\begin{itemize}
  \item High availability
  \item Low latency
  \item Massive scale
\end{itemize}

\begin{designbox}
We use a centralized ID generator to avoid collisions.
\end{designbox}

\section{High-Level Architecture}

\begin{tradeoff}
Centralized ID generation simplifies consistency but adds a bottleneck.
\end{tradeoff}

\begin{interviewtip}
Always clarify read/write ratio before choosing a datastore.
\end{interviewtip}

\begin{failuremode}
If the ID service goes down, URL creation halts completely.
\end{failuremode}
